{
  "configuration_id": "config_047",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_002 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, acc=0.6352). Across experiments, multiprofile >> singleprofile, imagenet_vit_l > resnet50, weighted > concat, and pca_n2000 >> scgpt. The one untested axis within this best-performing region is aggregation method: all top configs use avgpool, but transformer aggregation has not been paired with the optimal (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + weighted) combination. Question: Can transformer aggregation capture inter-profile interactions that avgpool misses, pushing accuracy above 0.635? Why this experiment: It is a minimal, logical extension of the current best (changing only aggregation), directly exploiting the strongest evidence while testing the most impactful remaining design choice. Expected cost: transformer aggregation adds moderate overhead over the ~7 GPU hours of config_002, so I estimate ~12–18 GPU hours—well within budget and far cheaper than the resnet50 multiprofile outlier (36.4). With 4 experiments remaining, this balances exploitation of the proven best region against the high-value uncertainty about aggregation architecture."
}

